window.docContents[99].resolve({"/Appendix/#section-chapter-7-colorings-results":{"contents":"* chromaticNumber_ne_top_of_finite: a graph on a finite vertex type has finite\nchromatic number.* Colorable.natCard_le_mul_indepNum / natCard_le_chromaticNumber_mul_indepNum:\na graph has at most χ G * ⍺ G vertices, since colour classes are\nindependent (trivially if V is infinite, when Nat.card V = 0).* Colorable.sup_of_isClique_inter / Colorable.sup_of_subsingleton_inter:\ncolourings of G₁ and G₂ from a common palette amalgamate to a colouring of\nG₁ ⊔ G₂ when the supports meet in a clique (in particular in at most one vertex).* blowUpGraph_colorable_iff: a blow-up of G with nonempty parts is k-colourable\niff G is.* Colorable.boxProd / colorable_boxProd_iff / chromaticNumber_boxProd:\nG □ H is k-colourable when both factors are (iff, for nonempty G and\nH), and χ (G □ H) = max (χ G) (χ H) for nonempty G and H.* hypercube_isBipartite / hypercube_cliqueFree_three: the hypercube Q[n] is\nbipartite, hence triangle-free.* colorable_mycielskian_succ_iff: G is k-colourable iff mμ[G] is\n(k + 1)-colourable.* chromaticNumber_mycielskian: χ mμ[G] = χ G + 1.* chromaticNumber_iterMycielskian /\nchromaticNumber_iterMycielskian_completeGraph_two: the n-th iterated\nMycielskian of G has chromatic number χ G + n, so that of K[2] has chromatic\nnumber n + 2.* mycielski: Mycielski's theorem, mμ^n K[2] has clique number 2 and chromatic\nnumber n + 2.* degree_le_chromaticNumber_lineGraph / maxDegree_le_chromaticNumber_lineGraph:\nthe chromatic index χ L[G] is at least the degree of every vertex, and so at\nleast Δ(G) for a finite graph.* greedy_lt / Adj.greedy_ne: the greedy colour of v is at most degreeLT v,\nand adjacent vertices receive different greedy colours.* colorable_of_degreeLT_le: the greedy bound for graphs on ℕ: if every vertex\nhas at most Δ earlier neighbours then the graph is\n(Δ + 1)-colourable.* crownGraph_neighborLTFinset / greedy_crownGraph_eq: in crownGraph the earlier\nneighbours of n are the n / 2 vertices of the other parity below n, and the\ngreedy colouring colours n with n / 2, the worst possible.* encode_degreeLT_le: degreeLT of an encoded vertex is at most the degree of the\noriginal vertex.* colorable_of_degree_le_of_countable: a locally finite graph on a countable vertex\ntype with all degrees at most Δ is (Δ + 1)-colourable.* greedyChoice_eq_greedyChoiceMin / greedyMemo_eq_greedy /\ngreedy_eq_greedyMemo: the Nat.find, Finset.min' and memoized greedy\ncolourings agree; the last is the @[csimp] lemma that makes #eval greedy run\nthe memoized version.\n\nFrom the exercises:\n\n* le_mul_of_colorable_kneserGraph: if the Kneser graph Kn[n, k] is\nm-colourable then n ≤ k * m, so χ Kn[n, k] ≥ n / k.\n\n","context":"Graph Theory in Lean\u0009Appendix\u0009Results","header":"14.3.5. Chapter 7: Colorings (Results)","id":"/Appendix/#section-chapter-7-colorings-results"}});